{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "pack": "expression-register",
  "title": "The Expression Register",
  "description": "Let Vim do the arithmetic: <C-r>= while typing, \\= in substitutions and :put = to generate lines.",
  "order": 11,
  "authors": ["navasvarela"],
  "levels": [
    {
      "id": "expr-01",
      "title": "Sign the release",
      "description": "The release notes need the SHA-256 of their first line on the checksum line. You can't type that from memory, and you don't have to.",
      "start_text": ["vimdojo 1.0 is ready to ship", "checksum: "],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "vimdojo 1.0 is ready to ship",
          "checksum: c48643711b8092d9d0cc9717a2e50ee89c0078dab85b4830a09751d2ed85a290"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 18,
      "par_seconds": 27,
      "hint": "In Insert mode, <C-r>= lets you type any expression and inserts its value. Try sha256(). The registers are variables in there: @\" is the one you just yanked into.",
      "solution": "y$jA<C-r>=sha256(@\")<CR><Esc>",
      "teaches": ["<C-r>=", "@\""]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-02",
      "title": "Lookup table",
      "description": "Add the squares of 1 to 20 below the comment, one per line.",
      "start_text": ["# Perfect squares, for the lookup table"],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "# Perfect squares, for the lookup table",
          "1",
          "4",
          "9",
          "16",
          "25",
          "36",
          "49",
          "64",
          "81",
          "100",
          "121",
          "144",
          "169",
          "196",
          "225",
          "256",
          "289",
          "324",
          "361",
          "400"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 32,
      "par_seconds": 48,
      "hint": ":put = puts the value of an expression below the cursor, and a list goes on one line per item. range() makes a list, and map() with a lambda like {_,v->v+1} changes every item. :put can be shortened to :pu.",
      "solution": ":pu=map(range(1,20),{_,v->v*v})<CR>",
      "teaches": [":put =", "map()"]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-03",
      "title": "Retina ready",
      "description": "Everything in this stylesheet doubles for high-density screens: double every px value. The z-index and the opacity are not sizes.",
      "start_text": [
        ".card {",
        "  margin: 8px 12px 16px 24px;",
        "  padding: 4px 6px;",
        "  width: 320px;",
        "  height: 180px;",
        "  z-index: 10;",
        "  opacity: 0.75;",
        "  border: 1px solid;",
        "}"
      ],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          ".card {",
          "  margin: 16px 24px 32px 48px;",
          "  padding: 8px 12px;",
          "  width: 640px;",
          "  height: 360px;",
          "  z-index: 10;",
          "  opacity: 0.75;",
          "  border: 2px solid;",
          "}"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 31,
      "par_seconds": 46,
      "hint": "A replacement starting with \\= is an expression. submatch(0) is the whole match, and it turns into a number when you do arithmetic with it. \\ze stops the match before the px.",
      "solution": ":%s/\\d*\\zepx/\\=submatch(0)*2/g<CR>",
      "teaches": ["\\=", "submatch()"]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-04",
      "title": "Where am I",
      "description": "Replace each __LINE__ with the number of the line it is on. __init__ and __name__ are fine as they are.",
      "start_text": [
        "def __init__(self):",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: starting\")",
        "    self.name = __name__",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: named\")",
        "",
        "def load(self):",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: loading\")",
        "    self.data = read()",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: read\")",
        "    self.parse()",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: parsed\")",
        "",
        "def __del__(self):",
        "    log(\"__LINE__: gone\")"
      ],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "def __init__(self):",
          "    log(\"2: starting\")",
          "    self.name = __name__",
          "    log(\"4: named\")",
          "",
          "def load(self):",
          "    log(\"7: loading\")",
          "    self.data = read()",
          "    log(\"9: read\")",
          "    self.parse()",
          "    log(\"11: parsed\")",
          "",
          "def __del__(self):",
          "    log(\"14: gone\")"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 23,
      "par_seconds": 34,
      "hint": "line('.') is the number of the line being substituted, even in a :%s.",
      "solution": ":%s/__L\\w*/\\=line('.')<CR>",
      "teaches": ["line('.')"]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-05",
      "title": "Special characters",
      "description": "Replace PREFIX with the path in register a everywhere it appears. The path holds both / and &, which mean something to :s, and pasting it with <C-r>a won't survive that.",
      "start_text": [
        "bin=PREFIX/bin",
        "lib=PREFIX/lib",
        "man=PREFIX/man",
        "etc=PREFIX/etc",
        "var=PREFIX/var",
        "doc=PREFIX/doc",
        "src=PREFIX/src",
        "tmp=PREFIX/tmp",
        "PATH=PREFIX/bin:PREFIX/tools:$PATH"
      ],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "bin=/opt/R&D/bin",
          "lib=/opt/R&D/lib",
          "man=/opt/R&D/man",
          "etc=/opt/R&D/etc",
          "var=/opt/R&D/var",
          "doc=/opt/R&D/doc",
          "src=/opt/R&D/src",
          "tmp=/opt/R&D/tmp",
          "PATH=/opt/R&D/bin:/opt/R&D/tools:$PATH"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 17,
      "par_seconds": 26,
      "hint": "An expression's value goes in literally, so nothing in it is special. @a reads register a.",
      "solution": ":%s/PR\\u*/\\=@a/g<CR>",
      "teaches": ["\\=@a"],
      "preset": {
        "registers": {
          "a": "/opt/R&D"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-06",
      "title": "Hex to decimal",
      "description": "Somebody pasted this from a debugger. Convert every 0x value to decimal.",
      "start_text": [
        "status=0x1F flags=0xA0",
        "mask=0xFF retries=0x3",
        "port=0x1F90 uid=0x3E8",
        "offset=0x10 size=0x400",
        "limit=0xC8 nice=0x13"
      ],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "status=31 flags=160",
          "mask=255 retries=3",
          "port=8080 uid=1000",
          "offset=16 size=1024",
          "limit=200 nice=19"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 26,
      "par_seconds": 39,
      "hint": "Vim reads a string like 0x1F as a number when it does arithmetic with it.",
      "solution": ":%s/0\\w*/\\=+submatch(0)/g<CR>",
      "teaches": ["unary +"]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-07",
      "title": "Count them for me",
      "description": "Each strncmp's last argument should be the length of its string. They all say 0. Let Vim count.",
      "start_text": [
        "strncmp(hdr, \"content-type\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"content-length\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"transfer-encoding\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"accept-language\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"if-none-match\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"x-forwarded-for\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"user-agent\", 0)",
        "strncmp(hdr, \"cache-control\", 0)"
      ],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "strncmp(hdr, \"content-type\", 12)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"content-length\", 14)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"transfer-encoding\", 17)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"accept-language\", 15)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"if-none-match\", 13)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"x-forwarded-for\", 15)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"user-agent\", 10)",
          "strncmp(hdr, \"cache-control\", 13)"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 38,
      "par_seconds": 57,
      "hint": "submatch(1) is the first group, even when \\zs leaves it outside the replaced text. len() counts the bytes of a string.",
      "solution": ":%s/\\v\"(.*)\", \\zs0/\\=len(submatch(1))<CR>",
      "teaches": ["submatch(1)", "len()"]
    },
    {
      "id": "expr-08",
      "title": "Twelve columns",
      "description": "Generate the widths of a twelve-column grid below the comment, as in the goal. Each width is its column's share of 100%, to two decimals.",
      "start_text": ["# column width"],
      "cursor_start": [1, 0],
      "goal": {
        "type": "buffer_equals",
        "value": [
          "# column width",
          "col1 8.33%",
          "col2 16.67%",
          "col3 25.00%",
          "col4 33.33%",
          "col5 41.67%",
          "col6 50.00%",
          "col7 58.33%",
          "col8 66.67%",
          "col9 75.00%",
          "col10 83.33%",
          "col11 91.67%",
          "col12 100.00%"
        ]
      },
      "par_keys": 60,
      "par_seconds": 90,
      "hint": "printf() does the formatting, and %% is a literal percent sign. v:val/0.12 is a float. In a map() lambda, the second argument is the item.",
      "solution": ":pu=map(range(1,12),{_,v->printf('col%d %.2f%%',v,v/0.12)})<CR>",
      "teaches": ["printf()"]
    }
  ]
}
